Package: anonify
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, nftables, iproute2, procps
Recommends: tor, wireguard-tools, network-manager, bubblewrap, curl, obfs4proxy
Description: temporary, reversible network privacy hardening
 anonify layers network-anonymity hardening on Linux and takes it back off
 again: randomized MAC and hostname, sysctl hardening, IPv6 and DNS leak
 prevention, Tor or WireGuard behind a fail-closed nftables kill switch,
 local discovery silencing, a read-only leak audit and a per-application
 sandbox.
 .
 All state lives in /run/anonify (tmpfs) and in kernel runtime state, so
 "anonify restore" or a reboot returns the machine to its original
 configuration. It never deletes, alters or suppresses logs, audit records,
 histories, timestamps or evidence, and it does not hide activity.
 .
 This package also ships anonify-browser, a portable helper that opens
 Firefox or LibreWolf with a throwaway, leak-hardened profile without root.
